    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0042" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-11T12:00:00+08:00">January 11,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 11—3:56 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. As possible indication French China policy is comment French Ambassador in
                    discussing Chinese request for mediation (our 61, January 8, and 62 January 9)
                    to effect that given repercussions Indochina of Communist regime in China,
                    French interest required supporting any regime in China resisting Communism.
                    This was true, he said, even though eventual collapse such resistance was
                    inevitable as France would at least gain time.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 73; repeated Paris 1.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
